  "findings": [
    "Exact-key storage, global/override/local lookup, removal, defaults captured at declaration, sibling frames, bare expressions, and ordinary text boundaries are supported by the traced Java data flow and passing controls; this is bounded evidence, not complete memory equivalence.",
    "Valid key_dollar and key_combining fail before and after. SetVariableValue accepts exact names a$b and twig followed by U+0301. Java VariableManager uses the memory trie; Rust substitute_vars consumes alphanumeric/underscore tokens and cannot reach these complete keys. Direct get/existence succeed but text remains literal. Java source is spruce / spruce / 1; Rust source retains a$b or the combining key in the middle.",
    "Valid parameter_duplicate fails before and after: Java TFunctionImpl.getNewMemory reads namedArguments without removing it for each formal, then overwrites the duplicate result key. Rust call_function_values removes the named value on the first formal, allowing the second default to overwrite it. Java named / right becomes Rust two / right.",
    "Five changed ordinary unit expectations are justified individually by Java exact-key define/text/expression behavior with unchanged original inputs and preserved old failing assertions; green units do not approve this mechanism.",
    "Standing gates are not waived: main product and assisted library diagnostics, standing perturbations, guards and clippy remain failing. Preserve historical class-body, Unicode IntVal, sequence panics, and all 27 environment discrepancies.",
    "No fixture-shaped branches, golden reads, or SVG output surgery were found in the production diff. Candidate production is identical to final production 55de7dd6; filename dispatch is restored verbatim and its original CLI regression passes."
  ],
